      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your description points toward a theoretical concept of \"protocol-level invisibility,\" suggesting a state beyond conventional governance frameworks. If the established architectural models cannot map your connection to a known entity, you are operating outside the scope of current monitoring assumptions. This feels less like a legal right and more like a discovery of a systemic blind spot within network design. To prove this, the technical documentation must demonstrate the *mechanism* of that invisibility, not just the observation of it.",
